  "limitations": [
    "Expanded component is the frozen-encoder-to-fast-MLP adapter, not the Qwen/vision backbone; the frozen visual representation remains the information bottleneck.",
    "pre200 versus pre800 changes both sampled training pairs and optimizer updates; the effect cannot be attributed to independent-data scale alone.",
    "The 32/64 readout diagnostics still use visual pretraining on all 111 train cases; they are low-label action-head diagnostics, not low-data end-to-end training.",
    "All scaling runs use one seed and reuse the previously inspected 57-case test split, so their test comparison is exploratory rather than confirmatory.",
    "The split has only two held-out recording days in test; small accuracy differences should not be interpreted as stable generalization without another untouched split."
  ]
